# Firebase. `google-services.json` carries the project's app id and API key;
# the key is restricted to the package name and signing certificate, so Google
# considers it safe to commit — but "safe if the restriction is correct" is not
# a property this repository can verify, and a credential is cheaper to hand
# over out of band than to un-publish. See docs/ops/push.md.
packages/client/android/app/google-services.json
# The service account private key. This one is not arguable.
#
# Both patterns matter: Firebase downloads these as
# `<project>-firebase-adminsdk-<hash>-<digits>.json`, which the first pattern
# alone would not have matched — so the obvious thing to do with the file
# straight out of the browser (drop it in the repo) would have committed it.
*service-account*.json

*firebase-adminsdk*.json
